# CPU (mean % of 32 cores) vs mean concurrency
# Source: docs/reports/moca-side-by-side-report.md
# All lines pass through the origin.
#
# Four data blocks, referenced as index 0..3 in gnuplot.
#
# Block 0: fc warm D=10% (measured)
# Block 1: fc warm D=2% (predicted)
# Block 2: fc perexec D=10% band (col2=noop floor, col3=real ceiling)
#           Real ceiling smoothed via queueing model: CPU = a*N / (1 - a*N/K)
#           fitted through (14, 19.6) and (40, 78.1):  a=1.215, K=128.6.
#           No-op floor is linear (0.275 %/sandbox, measured pre-knee).
# Block 3: fc perexec D=2% band (col2=noop floor, col3=real ceiling)
#           Linear (knee at N≈200+, far off chart).


